    "A graduate at the CBS median of 3,500 euros a month (wo, economics) gains nothing from the ruling if aged 30 or over or without a master's, and 198 euros a month if under 30 with a master's, because the floors are 48,013 and 36,497 euros a year [2, 4, 5].",
    "Living in the Netherlands during a master's normally fails the test of 16 of the previous 24 months more than 150 km away, and 42.1% of international graduates in the Nuffic cohorts still lived here one year after graduating [4, 6].",
